# id: BM12-no-buffer-cap
# blinds: the WAL-buffer tripwire
# covering-lane: cpp-test
# expect: killed
# control-lane: cpp-build
# expect-control: alive
#
# The catalogue's BM12. The buffer grows without bound.
#
# In a fault-injected harness that means an OOM kill, WHICH IS THE WORST
# POSSIBLE FAILURE SIGNAL because it destroys the run that would have explained
# it: no ledger, no kill point, no seed, just a dead process and a sweep that
# cannot say what it was doing. The tripwire's job is to make the run HALT with
# a status instead.
#
# The cap is a tripwire and not a policy. Status::kBusy as the policy remains
# the leaning for B5, and section 7.6.1's precondition is its acceptance test.
--- a/engine-cpp/src/wal/wal.cc	2026-08-24 21:15:11
+++ b/engine-cpp/src/wal/wal.cc	2026-08-24 21:15:11
@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@
 
   DbLock lock(mu_);
   if (closed_) return Status::InvalidArgument("Apply after Close");
